1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,051
For an older or low-vision person living alone,

2
00:00:03,051 --> 00:00:05,039
a video doorbell isn't much help:

3
00:00:05,039 --> 00:00:07,690
it shows a picture they can't easily see.

4
00:00:07,690 --> 00:00:09,015
Did a parcel arrive?

5
00:00:09,015 --> 00:00:10,341
Is it still outside?

6
00:00:10,341 --> 00:00:12,660
Who's in the driveway at 3 AM?

7
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:13,986
DoorSight answers those questions.

8
00:00:15,405 --> 00:00:17,554
DoorSight is a Ring-powered doorstep assistant.

9
00:00:17,554 --> 00:00:21,136
It watches Ring live video, understands what's at the door,

10
00:00:21,136 --> 00:00:25,433
and sends calm, accessible updates to the resident and alerts to a

11
00:00:25,433 --> 00:00:25,792
caregiver.

12
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:32,136
Frames come from Ring's live WebRTC stream.

13
00:00:32,136 --> 00:00:34,482
Open-vocabulary detection finds the parcel locally,

14
00:00:34,482 --> 00:00:38,391
and a Strands agent decides who to tell and why.

15
00:00:38,391 --> 00:00:39,955
Every step is recorded.

16
00:01:04,405 --> 00:01:05,629
One big button.

17
00:01:05,629 --> 00:01:08,076
No menus, nothing to read closely.

18
00:01:24,405 --> 00:01:27,432
A car at 3 AM is unusual for this home,

19
00:01:27,432 --> 00:01:29,247
based on its own visit pattern,

20
00:01:29,247 --> 00:01:31,971
so the caregiver gets an alert that explains why.

21
00:01:49,402 --> 00:01:53,269
A naive system would say the parcel was stolen just because a

22
00:01:53,269 --> 00:01:54,880
different camera saw no box.

23
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:58,747
DoorSight fingerprints the camera view and refuses to raise a false alarm.

24
00:01:58,747 --> 00:02:01,647
Its safety rules are enforced in the agent's tools,

25
00:02:01,647 --> 00:02:02,936
not just its prompt.

26
00:02:15,405 --> 00:02:18,495
Ring WHEP video and webhooks, YOLO-World locally,

27
00:02:18,495 --> 00:02:22,467
a Strands agent on Amazon Bedrock, DynamoDB for state,

28
00:02:22,467 --> 00:02:26,881
a private S3 bucket for snapshots, SNS for caregiver email,

29
00:02:26,881 --> 00:02:31,736
all under a least-privilege IAM user, with more than 260 tests.

30
00:02:36,405 --> 00:02:38,957
Ring's sandbox has one doorbell and no webhooks,

31
00:02:38,957 --> 00:02:42,784
so we built around what's real and logged twelve friction entries for

32
00:02:42,784 --> 00:02:43,741
the Ring team.

33
00:02:43,741 --> 00:02:46,931
DoorSight helps people stay independent at their own front door.
